# revdiff custom keybindings. Chezmoi-managed; canonical source at
# ~/Developer/N4M3Z/dotfiles/dot_config/revdiff/keybindings, deploys to
# ~/.config/revdiff/keybindings.
#
# Format: `map <key> <action>` adds a mapping, `unmap <key>` removes one.
# Overrides layer on top of defaults — only divergent mappings need to be
# listed here. Run `revdiff --dump-keys` for the full default set.

# Lowercase `b` for blame. Upstream binds `B` (Shift+b) because lowercase
# `b` is the vim "word-back" motion by convention, but revdiff's vim-motion
# preset doesn't actually claim `b` (only counts, gg, G, zz/zt/zb, ZZ/ZQ).
# Both `b` and `B` now toggle the blame gutter — no unmap needed.
map b toggle_blame

# gitui-style numbered view shortcuts. Each number maps to a major visual
# mode toggle (same actions as the lowercase letter equivalents, kept as
# additive shortcuts). Caveat: vim-motion's count prefix feature uses
# numbers (`5j` = down five lines), so these mappings shadow counts.
# Remove these four lines if you actively use vim counts.
map 1 toggle_tree
map 2 toggle_collapsed
map 3 annot_list
map 4 toggle_compact
